          "question": "Burning when I pass urine, plus a temperature and back pain since yesterday. How urgent is this, and what does guidance describe for treatment?",
          "answer": "Your symptoms of burning when passing urine, a fever, and back pain are concerning and warrant urgent medical evaluation. While they may not indicate an immediate emergency, conditions such as a urinary tract infection (UTI), particularly an upper tract infection like pyelonephritis, may be present and require attention.\n\nAccording to the diagnostic specialist, these symptoms suggest a possible urinary tract infection, which can involve serious conditions even if the urgency isn't immediately clear. Additionally, the presence of fever and back pain elevates the seriousness of the situation, indicating the need for prompt medical attention.\n\nThe treatment guidelines from the research specialist indicate that uncomplicated UTIs may be treated empirically if typical symptoms are present, but in cases of complicated infections—especially those accompanied by fever or back pain—a different treatment plan and antibiotic regimen are necessary. Consulting a healthcare provider will help ensure an accurate diagnosis and the right treatment for your condition.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
